>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `REFUTE_TAC_WITH`

``` hol4
Refute.REFUTE_TAC_WITH : config_update list -> Abbrev.tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Searches for a counterexample under per-call configuration updates.

`REFUTE_TAC_WITH updates` is `REFUTE_CONFIG_TAC (current_config updates)`
with the configuration computed when the tactic is applied: the
`config -> config` updates are applied to `!Refute.the_config` from left
to right, so the last update of a field wins, and `the_config` itself is
not modified.  This is the way to change options for one call:

``` hol4
REFUTE_TAC_WITH
  [upd_search (Only [Narrowing]),
   upd_size 7,
   upd_timeout 5.0]
```

Like every Refute tactic it prints its `Counterexample`,
`NoCounterexample`, or `Unknown` report and then behaves as `ALL_TAC`,
never closing or altering the goal; every field of the resulting
configuration is honoured, including `quiet` and `expect`.

`REFUTE_TAC` is `REFUTE_TAC_WITH []`; `QUICKCHECK_TAC`, `NARROWING_TAC`,
and `MODEL_REFUTE_TAC` are `REFUTE_TAC_WITH [upd_search s]` for `s` equal
to `QuickcheckBackends`, `Only [Narrowing]`, and `Only [ModelFinder]`
respectively.  Use `Refute.REFUTE_CONFIG_TAC` where the result must not
depend on the session's interactive defaults at all.

### Failure

Fails only when a non-default `expect` field is not met.  An invalid
update raises when the updater is built, not when the tactic runs;
`upd_search (Only [])` is rejected this way.  Interrupts are re-raised.

